# enforcement-map-derivations and its shard driver (b, which execs the parent's run.sh --group) share ONE declaration.
# seed.sh copies core/, scripts/, .githooks/ and templates/ whole and mutates the copies; the validator then walks them.
# The validator under test, REQUIRED: the sentinel prints where run.sh passes its distribution-only guard.
!scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
scripts/
.githooks/
templates/
# reason: core/ is copied whole -- cp -R "$D_ROOT/core", core/fixtures/enforcement-map-derivations/seed.sh:31; the enforcement-map validator then walks the copy by content.
core/
